// the image generator spellcast3d-config.ini picks (Qwen-Image 2.1 built in, or Forge Neo with the artist's own
// models) from the words, the example pictures, and what the viewport shows: the picture with the marks painted over
// it (marks.js), or the black canvas that stands in for a picture. The picture can be sliced into the object's views
// (slicer.js, its buttons in the header). The prop's pictures stand in a row under the picture (tilerow.js), the
// oldest first; each has an × that takes it out of the prop, and Ctrl+Z brings it back; Alt + click on one shows what
// Qwen-Image was given for it (given.js). While Qwen-Image 2.1 draws, a rough preview shows in the picture's place
// after every step - over the part of it a window is drawn in, when it draws one.
// An empty draft (the next prop) first offers the ways as big cards; the one picked flies to the top right, where it
// becomes the mode control. The hub makes the draft a prop as soon as it has its first picture; the workbench stays
// on it. "+ New prop" brings the next, empty draft.

